//! A small board in a case of two models for the recipe `pcb-3d-case-colour` (issue #756): the
//! base states its colour, `.base.color &= Color::Blue`, over a file that has none; the lid
//! states none and its file styles its solid `#cc3366`, so it is drawn in the file's own colour.
//! `case_colour_3d/lid.step` is `case_fit/lid.step` with that style added.

import std::parts::connector::Header1x2
import std::mfg::jlcpcb::TwoLayer

board Tinted {
    .process: TwoLayer {
        .stackup.thickness &= 1.6mm
    }
    .power_in: Header1x2
}
